{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0.0) or shows early signs of decline.",
    "Reduce forecast peaks by 5-15% after a spike in price, especially if true outcome shows mean reversion or downward correction.",
    "If model overestimates price in early days of a new trend (e.g., after a low), apply a lag correction by reducing forecast by 10-20% for the next 3-5 days.",
    "When true outcome is significantly below model forecast (e.g., >15% error), apply a mean reversion bias: adjust forecast toward recent 5-day average.",
    "For sentiment = 0.0, assume neutral market; use historical 15-day average as baseline, but apply a 5% downward bias if true outcome is consistently lower than forecast.",
    "If true outcome shows a sharp drop after a high forecast, apply a ‘sudden reversal’ correction: reduce forecast by 10-25% for the next 2-3 days."
  ]
}
